<article class="env-lemma" id="0BLM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BLM">Lemma <span data-tag="0BLM">58.20.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0BLF" data-tag="0BLF">58.19.1</a>. Let $V$ be finite étale over $U$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ has depth $\geq 3$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$V_0 = V \times _ U U_0$ is equal to $Y_0 \times _{X_0} U_0$ for some $Y_0 \to X_0$ finite étale. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $V = Y \times _ X U$ for some $Y \to X$ finite étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption of depth forces $H^1_\mathfrak m(A) = H^2_\mathfrak m(A) = 0$, see Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AVZ" data-tag="0AVZ">47.11.1</a>. Hence Lemma <a href="/tag/0BLS" data-tag="0BLS">58.20.6</a> applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>